WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.890
Let's go, cleanup!

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.600
Need a run here!

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.480
<i>He has really good control.</i>

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:11.110
His timing's still off.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.240
Inashiro's batters struggled against him.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.620
He uses his fast and slow 
pitches really well.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.120
Not to mention,

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.370
he still has another pitch up his sleeve.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.210
Foul!

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.250
Ume-chan, finish it!

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.720
<i>Damn.</i>

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.220
<i>No matter where I pitch...</i>

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.510
Ball.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.510
Yes! Nice one!

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.770
<i>Shoot, it slipped a bit.</i>

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.270
<i>Full count now.</i>

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.270
<i>We're three runs behind.</i>

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:50.780
<i>As the cleanup, I can't go down 
without putting up a fight.</i>

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.610
<i>Or the entire team</i>

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:58.200
<i>will think this pitcher is hard to face.</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.540
<i>Miyuki.</i>

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.420
<i>I don't care about this captain 
and vice captain stuff,</i>

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.380
<i>but as players who play on the field,</i>

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.930
<i>we can prove ourselves 
through how we play.</i>

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.520
<i>In order to relieve the 
tension in the team,</i>

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.400
<i>you have to get a hit.</i>

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.110
<i>I'm sure they watched 
our game against Inashiro.</i>

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.200
Guess there's no point in holding back.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:41.910
<i>I should</i>

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.910
<i>take him out with my full strength.</i>

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.250
<i>I'll end it</i>

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.050
<i>with my power curveball!</i>

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.480
<i>The slider?</i>

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:48.450
<b>Persistent and Diligent</b>

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.700
Guess there's no point in holding back.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.080
<i>I should</i>

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.830
<i>take him out with my full strength.</i>

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.500
<i>I'll end it</i>

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.590
<i>with my power curveball!</i>

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.260
<i>The slider?</i>

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.570
Nice! Straight through center!

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:22.610
Go! Go!

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.120
Yeah!

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.620
Second base runner scores!

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.450
Time for a comeback!

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.250
That's how you do it!

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.120
About time you learned!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.880
You're next, Zono!

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.960
<i>Damn.</i>

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.630
<i>He reacted well.</i>

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.630
<i>It was a lot sharper than I expected.</i>

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:49.640
<i>I owe Nabe for getting it 
on video yesterday.</i>

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:53.770
It looked like he reacted quickly 
 to an unexpected pitch.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.350
He smacked the other team's ace's best pitch.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.320
That's how a cleanup should bat.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:04.780
<b>Ugumori

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.780
The wind that was blowing in 
Ugumori's favor is gone now.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.110
Ye—

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:07.820
Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:09.160
Yes! Yes!

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.540
You took my line!

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.160
Let's go, Zono!

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.790
<i>He got a hit under immense pressure,</i>

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:24.420
<i>and got Furuya back into the game
 with one word on the field.</i>

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:27.550
<i>I have to admit it.</i>

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:30.470
<i>He's head and shoulders 
above the rest of us.</i>

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.560
<i>But that's the reason.</i>

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.070
<i>It's because he's such an amazing player...</i>

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:48.820
<i>...that I got so pissed.</i>

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:54.120
Going deep into left field!

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.750
Miyuki, run for it!

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.080
Two RBIs in a row!

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.080
Let's go!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:04.170
So many runs in just the first inning.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.170
Both teams' cleanups did their jobs well.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:11.350
<b>Ugumori

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:16.520
Out!

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.890
Let's go!

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.650
<i>That change of pace.</i>

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.650
Just one run short now!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.280
Nice job, Zono!

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.530
That was the legendary Zono Double!

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.320
Zono.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.350
I owe it to you for smacking his slider.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.310
I could see his fastball coming.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.560
<i>We may all hold different values,</i>

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.690
<i>but we're all playing the same game.</i>

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.730
<i>We want to win the fall tournament 
and take the coach to nationals.</i>

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:10.400
<i>That's one goal we all have in common.</i>

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.410
This inning's important!

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:17.040
Let's defend well and get back to offense.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.200
Furuya, one out at a time!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.040
See? There wasn't a problem.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.210
Yeah.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:24.920
Time to prepare for the worst!

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:35.220
Fierce

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:27.670
Amateurs don't have slumps!

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.760
No matter how well you do, 
you're all still just amateurs!

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.340
Amateurs!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.140
Don't try to do what you can't do!

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:35.220
Just do what you can, the best you can!

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.390
Shut up!

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:37.720
You're ruining the atmosphere!

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.390
You read Nomu-san's book 
yesterday, didn't you?

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.520
Run out there with energy, boys!

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:47.570
I was worried after Furuya 
gave up the home run,

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:50.190
but the team looks pretty calm.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:53.160
It must be because of Miyuki's RBI.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.740
It fueled the fire to fight back.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:03.120
After Furuya gave up the home run, 
what did he tell him?

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.250
That's what I want to know.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:31.610
Fukui.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.740
Take Tadano to watch 
the game at Edogawa.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.530
The Seido vs. Ugumori game?

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:43.290
It's not exactly pleasing to watch 
the game you wanted to play,

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:46.000
but you'll learn a lot.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.880
<i>Maybe the coach wanted</i>

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:53.340
<i>to show Tadano how Miyuki plays
 not just this one game.</i>

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:59.510
Let's just see how the game will play out.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:04.940
<b>Ugumori
Seido</b>

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.890
Let's go, Ume-chan!

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:04.940
Come on!

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.190
Nice pitch!

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.220
Strike! Batter out!

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.300
Nice, Furuya!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.760
Nice pitch!

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.230
The Seido battery pitched a lot of splitters.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:50.060
He smacked a fastball over the fence 
the last time he was up to bat.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:55.400
<i>I hope that made him think 
about breaking balls.</i>

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.080
Nice try, Ume-chan!

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.710
You can't hit 'em all!

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:10.130
Good try, Ume-chan!

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.340
Feel better, Ume-chan!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.210
You don't need to cheer me up!

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:17.590
Seido saw how Inashiro lost, 
so they're being cautious.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:21.090
We should forget 
about the lead we have.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.970
It's never been on my mind.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:30.350
A challenger can't take the belt 
if he goes on the defensive.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:42.200
Come on!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.280
Go all the way!

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.710
It's gone!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:53.250
A two-run homer into 
the right field!

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:55.750
W-Wow!

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.380
Damn.

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.390
<b>Missed it</b>

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:04.300
That's his third run this game!

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:08.270
What a catcher, 
to pay back the pitcher's debt!

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:21.280
Edogawa City Stadium

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:31.790
<b>Ugumori

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.570
Nice! Sixth run!

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.780
Our batters are on fire!

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.780
Let's go!

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:04.280
Are you an Aries, Zono-san?

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.200
They have the best luck today!

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.120
Your lucky item is a rubber hose!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.160
Nice hit!

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:11.960
Who is that?

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:12.910
Zono!

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.960
Nice one, Zono!

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:22.880
Umemiya-kun pitched an entire game 
against Inashiro yesterday,

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.680
so maybe he's fatigued from that game.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:28.760
It's become rather one-sided.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:31.020
I thought they had 
better batters last year,

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:32.810
but they're really good.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:37.730
I wish I could've seen 
a Seido vs. Inashiro game.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.320
Totally.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:46.280
<i>What's wrong, pompadour?</i>

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.120
<i>Already knocked out?</i>

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.830
Batting sixth and pitcher, Furuya-kun.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:55.670
Furuya!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.580
Hit it, Furuya!

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:01.340
<i>Furuya, this is where you 
deal the finishing blow.</i>

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:12.520
Second!

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:14.680
I'll cover!

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:15.520
Leave it to me!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.360
We won't lose.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:26.240
Out!

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:28.160
Nice double play!

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:29.820
Let's go!

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:31.370
Let's go!

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:45.920
<b>Ugumori
Seido</b>

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:58.230
Ball!

00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:59.600
Nice pass!

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:01.980
They're persistent.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:03.070
Yes.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:06.780
Furuya-kun's been forced 
to pitch a lot from the beginning.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:11.700
<i>They're making it harder 
by not swining at the low pitches.</i>

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.450
<i>But you're pitching well.</i>

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:18.290
<i>Don't lose focus.</i>

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.380
Into right field!

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:30.760
Nice hit!

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.600
We have a man on first now!

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:47.860
Steal!

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.620
Out!

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.710
Another steal attempt foiled!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.250
Nice one, Miyuki!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:06.300
You won't steal that easily!

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:09.550
Not against this guy!

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:18.890
It's not the best idea 
to steal while he's catching.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.730
I commend them for trying,

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:26.690
but aren't they forcing it a bit?

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.280
Yeah.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:34.280
This offensive strategy 
raises morale when it works,

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:37.540
but it can be devastating when it fails.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:42.290
Especially as the game progresses, 
these plays become detrimental.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.130
Your start was pretty good.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.420
Damn it.

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.130
Only the start, though.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:50.920
Shut up!

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:55.930
But why does Ugumori look so cheerful?

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.310
Nishi-yan, you've got this!

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:00.180
Hit the first pitch!

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:04.060
<b>Warming Up Every Inning</b>

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.060
We can't relax yet.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.060
He doesn't have stamina.

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:34.930
Wow!

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.340
The runner couldn't get back!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.470
Nice double play!

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:40.560
Nice pitch, Furuya!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.100
Nice pitch!

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:46.730
Ugumori got runners on base,

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:49.820
but couldn't score again.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:54.240
Furuya-kun hasn't allowed 
a run since the first inning,

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.360
so it looks like he's already recovered.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.370
Furuya, nice pitch!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:02.500
<i>He's still throwing well, 
but his pitch count is over 100 now.</i>

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.920
<i>We should think about 
switching him out soon.</i>

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:09.500
<b>Ugumori
Seido</b>

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.760
Ume-chan, two outs!

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:14.630
Two outs!

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:20.390
Bottom of the sixth,

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:23.350
two outs and bases loaded 
from hits and errors.

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:27.020
And Kominato-kun's up to bat.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:30.270
Seido could score again.

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:33.280
This is where you become a man!

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:35.530
From Haruichi to Haruo!

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.530
Haruo?

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:41.030
Let's go, Kominato!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.710
He laughed?

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:49.960
Between first and second!

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:57.260
All right! Three outs!

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.550
Nice defense!

00:17:58.550 --> 00:17:59.970
It's not over yet!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.100
That was magnificent.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.390
Yeah.

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:06.100
Any more runs would've ended the game.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.890
What's wrong, first-years?

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:09.730
You're all dead weight!

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.110
Nice one, Mako-chan!
 You really came through!

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:18.360
Man, these batters are so persistent, 
I'm getting tired.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:21.570
They don't swing at any balls.

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:23.450
And they all swing compactly.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.330
Yeah.

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:29.830
But I have to say,

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:33.170
playing against strong opponents is fun.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.840
It's so stimulating and suspenseful.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:42.600
There's nothing to worry about 
if you're enjoying this game.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.930
We have three more innings!

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.230
Let's score and score 
and score and score!

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:50.810
Yeah!

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:54.360
<b>Ugumori
Seido</b>

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:02.700
Safe!

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:05.700
Nice!

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.410
Our lead-off man's fast, too!

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:11.170
Damn.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.380
You think he'll steal?

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:21.050
I don't know.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:23.300
Miyuki-kun's been getting...

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:28.890
He's going!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.320
Safe!

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.330
It's the top of the seventh!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.830
It's time for payback!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:48.740
Come on!

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:49.950
Yeah!

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.120
Let's do this!

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.640
It looks like my time has come!

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:06.720
Give me a second!

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:13.060
<i>Pitch low and carefully.</i>

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:31.200
<i>Into that mitt.</i>

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:39.340
Yeah!

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:41.090
Out!

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.630
Got him!

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.640
Strike!

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.430
Nice pitch, Furuya!

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:49.890
Nice pitch!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:57.350
<i>He's relaxed and swinging 
his arm down all the way.</i>

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:03.240
<i>Are his pitches getting better?</i>

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:13.370
I wonder if Furuya-kun has switched 
to pitching to contact.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:16.460
He's pitching low strikes consistently,

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.920
so the Ugumori batters 
are forced to swing.

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:25.050
It looks like he's pitching 
very carefully rather than all out.

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.640
<i>This is troubling.</i>

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.470
<i>He's a lot more persistent than I thought.</i>

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:37.190
<i>I thought he'd break down by now.</i>

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:45.780
Strike! Batter out!

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:50.370
The ace Furuya is persistent and diligent!

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.290
He's not fazed by the pinch at all!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:57.040
Nice pitch, Furuya!

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:58.290
Nice pitch!

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:32.930
The end of the game is approaching.

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:34.510
Furuya just might pitch till the end.

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:37.970
But why are they so cheerful 
despite being down in runs?

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:40.060
Wh-What's with the crowd's reaction?

00:23:40.430 --> 00:23:44.810
We're being engulfed by something 
outside of our control.

00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:46.320
This is bad!

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:47.190
Furuya, switch out!

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:48.570
Switch right now!

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:51.950
Next time on <i>Ace of the Diamond Season 2</i>:
Chain Reaction.

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:54.950
<b>Chain Reaction</b>

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:53.950
Let's win the national title!
